## Watch the task, then inspect the design

![Recorded forward-kinematics pick-and-place task](02_Simulation_and_Animation/Trajectories/pick_place_fk.gif)

The 9.24 s demonstration approaches, grasps, transfers and releases an object. The browser viewer animates the actual CAD meshes and can isolate every part. The GIF above is a forward-kinematics line view; object attachment is idealized in the simulation.

**Inspect online:** [move and isolate the robot](https://pratham-cloud-ctrl.github.io/INDRBT/#robot), [search the PCB and highlight nets](https://pratham-cloud-ctrl.github.io/INDRBT/#pcb), or [rotate the native 3D board](https://pratham-cloud-ctrl.github.io/INDRBT/#pcb3d). GitHub can decline previews of CAD files; the public showcase serves the actual display assets directly.

**For optional offline use:** [download the current repository](https://github.com/pratham-cloud-ctrl/INDRBT/archive/refs/heads/main.zip), extract it and open **OPEN_3D_VIEWER.cmd** on Windows. On any system, open `02_Simulation_and_Animation/Interactive_3D_Viewer.html` in a browser. It provides a local copy of the joint controls, part isolation and playback available online. GitHub shows this HTML source rather than executing it.

